  "limits": "Action executor uses actual submit, scope abort, owner/program/admission/retirement/selector. Progress step and successful parsed responses remain explicit controlled boundaries in new action cases. Separate external driver pin/root is modeled and asserted. Actual client-mark-dead/progress-abort, transport/session/codec abort, per-owner close and physical operation destructor, final pool-destruction helper, request/FID/pool/CQ transitions. Parsed successful replies remain synthetic; prior preparation regressions never submit. Host native teardown, translation, allocator, image snapshot, ref/engine/wake and physical backing drop boundaries. Earlier preparation/provided cases retain manual fixture destruction; new retirement cases use actual destructor. Final pool helper is called at simulated zero Loom references, not actual retirer. No native READY/frontend/close/concurrency qualification."
